Q: How to cleanly compare two time values (either of which might be empty) A: <p>This is your code for your <code>Version 2</code>and how you can make some modification to make it works :</p>

<pre><code>$aData = $this-&gt;get($memberA);
$bData = $this-&gt;get($memberB); 

// You create two empty string for the date you want to compare
$aDatetime = "";
$bDatetime = "";    

// You check if both data are not empty and if updateTime is defined
if (!empty($aData) &amp;&amp; isset($aData['updateTime'])) {
    $aDatetime = new DateTime($aData['updateTime']);
} else {
    $aDatetime = new DateTime('1970-01-01');
}
if (!empty($bData) &amp;&amp; isset($bData['updateTime'])) {
    $bDatetime = new DateTime($bData['updateTime']);
} else {
    $bDatetime = new DateTime('1970-01-01');
}    
</code></pre>

<p>What you did before :</p>

<ul>
<li>You echo 'A' if <code>$bData</code> is empty AND <code>$aData</code> is not empty</li>
<li>You echo 'A' if <code>$aData['updateTime'] &gt;= $bData['updateTime']</code></li>
<li>You echo 'B' if <code>$aData</code> is empty AND <code>$bData</code> is not empty</li>
<li>You echo 'B' if <code>$aData['updateTime'] &lt; $bData['updateTime']</code></li>
<li>You echo '' if both <code>$aData</code> AND <code>$bData</code> are empty</li>
</ul>

<p>You can do it with THREE condition now :</p>

<pre><code>// Echo A if $aData['updateTime'] &gt;= $bData['updateTime'] as before
// If $bData is empty, now it's a datetime for date 1970-01-01 so still true
// Add condition to check if $aDatetime is not '1970-01-01' to avoid case both data are empty
if ($aDatetime &gt;= $bDatetime &amp;&amp; $aDatetime-&gt;format('Y-m-d') !== '1970-01-01') {
    echo "A" ; 
// Echo B if $aData['updateTime'] &lt; $bData['updateTime'] as before
// If $aData is empty, now it's a datetime for date 1970-01-01 so still true
} else if ($aDatetime &lt; $bDatetime) {
    echo "B"; 
// This is the case where $aDatetime == $bDatetime and both are '1970-01-01' so both empty
} else {
    echo '';
}
</code></pre>

<p>Output with date test :</p>

<ul>
<li><code>$aData = '2018-10-23' &amp;&amp; $bData = '2018-10-23'</code> : echo A</li>
<li><code>$aData = '2018-10-23' &amp;&amp; $bData = '2018-10-20'</code> : echo A</li>
<li><code>$aData = '2018-10-20' &amp;&amp; $bData = ''</code> : echo A</li>
<li><code>$aData = '2018-10-20' &amp;&amp; $bData = '2018-10-23'</code> : echo B</li>
<li><code>$aData = '' &amp;&amp; $bData = '2018-10-20'</code> : echo B</li>
<li><code>$aData = '' &amp;&amp; $bData = ''</code> : echo ''</li>
</ul>
